  "findings": [
    {
      "title": "[P1] Update resolve() for Registry.lookup's versioned return shape",
      "body": "`Registry.lookup` now returns `{ payload: string; revision: number } | null` (`src/registry.ts:2-3`), but `src/resolve.ts:3` still does `if (cached) return JSON.parse(cached);`. On any cache hit the truthy envelope object is coerced to `\"[object Object]\"` and `JSON.parse` throws `SyntaxError` — every previously-working cached lookup path now fails instead of returning data, and the throw happens before the `remote.resolve` fallback. Under TypeScript this is also a type error (`JSON.parse` requires `string`). Fix by unwrapping the payload, e.g. `JSON.parse(cached.payload)`, or by keeping `lookup`'s string contract.",
      "severity": "P1",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/resolve.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 3,
        "end": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Store implementing only read() no longer works with lookup",
      "body": "The diff swaps `this.store.read(key)` for `this.store.readVersioned(key)` in `Registry.lookup` (`src/registry.ts:3`). The repo contains no store definition or adapter providing `readVersioned`, so any store wired in with the previously sufficient `read(key)` interface now fails every lookup with `TypeError: this.store.readVersioned is not a function`. Either provide a versioned store/adapter in this PR or keep a `read`-based fallback.",
      "severity": "P2",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/registry.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 3,
        "end": 3
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Remove ~4,400 duplicated filler comment lines",
      "body": "`src/registry.ts:4-2203` and `src/resolve.ts:4-2203` add ~2,200 identical numbered \"compatibility note\" comments each (~350 KB, growing each module ~1,500×). They carry no information, bury the real behavioral change at the top of each file (which is how a breaking contract edit hides inside a \"preserve contracts\" PR), and inflate every compile/lint/IDE/checkout scan and any comment-preserving build output. Worth confirming this padding is accidental (e.g. a codegen artifact) rather than intentional.",
      "severity": "P2",
      "location": {
        "path": "src/registry.ts",
        "side": "RIGHT",
        "start": 4,
        "end": 6
      }
    }
  ],
